4. Completion of the proof\n\nWe have shown:\n\n* No configuration can have more than \\(n\\) sunny lines (inequality (2)).\n* For each \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n-1\\) a configuration exists by the inductive construction of Section 2.\n* For \\(k=n\\) a configuration exists by the explicit family (3) of Section 3.\n\nTherefore the set of all admissible numbers of sunny lines is exactly  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n\\}} .\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
