\) passes through the lattice point \\((t,1)\\) and through all points of the form \\((t+u-1,u)\\) with \\(u\\ge1\\).  \nA point \\((a,b)\\) with \\(b\\le k\\) satisfies \\(a-b+1\\in\\{1,\\dots ,n\\}\\). If \\(a-b+1\\le k\\) then \\((a,b)\\) lies on the line \\(S_{a-b+1}\\).  \nThus the family \\(\\{S_t\\}_{t=1}^{k}\\) certainly covers all points of \\(T_n\\) whose ordinate \\(b\\) is at most \\(k\\) **and** whose difference \\(a-b\\) does not exceed \\(k-1\\).\n\nTo handle the remaining points we would like to add \\(n-k\\) non‑sunny lines (for instance horizontal lines). However, points with \\(b\\le k\\) but \\(a-b+1>k\\) cannot be covered by any of the horizontal lines \\(y=j\\) with \\(j\\ge k+1\\), because their ordinate is \\(\\le k\\). Consequently the above family does **not** guarantee a covering of all points of \\(T_n\\) for arbitrary \\(k\\).\n\n*Conclusion.*  \nWe have proved the necessary condition \\(k\\le n\\) and exhibited explicit configurations for the extreme values \\(k=0\\) and \\(k=n\\). The existence of configurations for the intermediate values \\(0<k<n\\) remains unresolved; the simple construction using only slope‑\\(1\\) sunny lines fails to cover all required lattice points. Further work is needed to either produce a valid construction for each such \\(k\\) or to show that some intermediate values are impossible.\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
