ecessary condition (Lemma 4) with the explicit constructions of §3, we have shown that\n\n\\[\nk\\text{ is admissible } \\Longleftrightarrow \n\\Bigl\\lceil\\frac{n+1}{2}\\Bigr\\rceil\\le k\\le n .\n\\]\n\nHence the set of all non‑negative integers \\(k\\) for which the required configuration exists is precisely the interval stated above.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\displaystyle \n\\Bigl\\lceil\\frac{n+1}{2}\\Bigr\\rceil,\\;\n\\Bigl\\lceil\\frac{n+1}{2}\\Bigr\\rceil+1,\\;\\dots ,\\; n } .\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
