point \\((a,b)\\in T_k\\).  Write \\(a=n-k+i\\) for the unique\n\\(i\\in\\{1,\\dots ,k\\}\\) determined by the \\(x\\)-coordinate, and set\n\\(b=k+1-i-j\\) with \\(j\\in\\{0,\\dots ,k-i\\}\\).  Substituting \\(a\\) into (5) gives\n\n\\[\ny = -\\frac{i}{k-i+1}(n-k+i) + \\frac{(n+1)k}{k-i+1}\n   = k+1-i-j = b .\n\\]\n\nThus \\((a,b)\\) satisfies the equation of \\(L_i\\); consequently every point of\n\\(T_k\\) lies on exactly one of the lines \\(\\{L_i\\}_{i=1}^{k}\\).\n\n#### 2.3  The whole family\n\nCollect the \\(n-k\\) vertical lines \\(V_j\\) and the \\(k\\) sunny lines \\(L_i\\).\nThe total number of lines is \\(n\\).  By construction:\n\n* every point of \\(S_n\\) belongs either to the vertical backbone (if its\n  \\(x\\)-coordinate \\(\\le n-k\\)) or to \\(T_k\\) (if its \\(x\\)-coordinate \\(\\ge\n  n-k+1\\)), and in the latter case it lies on the appropriate sunny line;\n* exactly \\(k\\) of the lines are sunny (the \\(L_i\\)\u2019s), the remaining\n  \\(n-k\\) are vertical and therefore non\u2011sunny.\n\nHence a configuration satisfying the two required conditions exists for the\nchosen \\(k\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 3.  Final classification\n\nWe have shown:\n\n* For every \\(n\\ge3\\) a configuration with \\(k=0\\) exists.\n* For every \\(n\\ge3\\) a configuration with any prescribed \\(k\\) satisfying\n  \\(1\\le k\\le n-1\\) exists (construction above).\n* No configuration with \\(k=n\\) exists (Lemma\u202f1 and the counting argument).\n\nTherefore the set of admissible values of \\(k\\) is precisely  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n-1\\}} .\n\\]"
