the set \\(T_n\\) contains strictly more points than can possibly be covered by \\(n\\) non‑sunny lines, contradicting the assumption that the \\(n\\) lines cover every point of \\(T_n\\).\n\nTherefore our initial assumption is false: **at least one of the \\(n\\) lines must be sunny**.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{k\\ge 1\\text{ for all }n\\ge 3}.\n\\]\n\nThis establishes a necessary condition on the admissible values of \\(k\\). The determination of all possible \\(k\\) remains open."
