lines is \\(n\\) and the number of sunny lines is precisely \\(k\\).\n\nSince the construction works for every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\), all these values are attainable.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### Exhaustiveness\n\nThe problem asks for *all* non‑negative integers \\(k\\) for which such a configuration exists.  \nWe have exhibited, for each \\(k\\) in the interval \\([0,n]\\), an explicit configuration satisfying the two required properties.  \nConversely, a configuration cannot contain more than \\(n\\) lines, so the number of sunny lines cannot exceed \\(n\\).  \nThus the set of admissible \\(k\\) is exactly \\(\\{0,1,\\dots ,n\\}\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n**Final Answer**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{For every }n\\ge 3\\text{, the possible values of }k\\text{ are }0,1,2,\\dots ,n.}\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
